    {
      "name": "NvdSsvcMetricV203",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcMetricV203",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "cve_api_json_2.0.schema#/definitions/ssvc-v203",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "A Stakeholder-Specific Vulnerability Categorization (SSVC) decision and who made it.",
      "comments": [
        "SPDX records the outcome of an SSVC decision, and NVD the path to it, so the mapping is only a related one."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "aliases": [
        "ssvc-v203"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "spdx3:Security/SsvcVulnAssessmentRelationship"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "NvdSsvcMetricV203_source",
        "nvdSsvcMetricV203__ssvcData"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "ssvcData",
          "description": "The decision.",
          "range": "NvdSsvcData",
          "required": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcMetricV203",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdSsvcData",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcData",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "ssvc-v2.0.3.json#",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "One SSVC decision, as the answers chosen on the way through a decision tree.",
      "comments": [
        "This class renders the structure of NVD's ssvc-v2.0.3.json. NVD's file also names a $schema key, which LinkML's Python generators cannot spell. No record of the modified feed of 2026-11-03 holds it, and tests/test_upstream.py lists the departure."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "slots": [
        "timestamp",
        "nvdSsvcData__computed",
        "nvdSsvcData__options",
        "nvdSsvcData__role",
        "nvdSsvcData__version",
        "nvdSsvcData__decisionTree",
        "nvdSsvcData__id",
        "nvdSsvcData__decisionTreeUrl",
        "nvdSsvcData__generator"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "computed",
          "description": "The decision in a short form.",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "options",
          "description": "The answers given, each as a decision point and its value.",
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "range": "NvdSsvcOption",
          "required": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "inlined_as_list": true,
          "minimum_cardinality": 1,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "role",
          "description": "The role of whoever made the decision, such as CISA Coordinator.",
          "required": true,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "version",
          "description": "The version of SSVC used.",
          "slot_uri": "nist_nvd:ssvcVersion",
          "required": true,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "decisionTree",
          "description": "The whole decision tree that was used.",
          "range": "NvdSsvcDecisionTree",
          "inlined": true,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "id",
          "description": "The vulnerability the decision is about, by whatever identifier.",
          "slot_uri": "nist_nvd:ssvcSubject",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "decisionTreeUrl",
          "description": "The address of the decision tree that was used.",
          "range": "uri",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "generator",
          "description": "The tool that wrote this decision.",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcData",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdSsvcOption",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcOption",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "ssvc-v2.0.3.json#/properties/options/items",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "One answer on the way through a decision tree, keyed by its decision point.",
      "comments": [
        "NVD's file allows any key, with a string or a list of strings as its value, and extra_slots states that. The real data holds one key per object, and only these three, each with a string. They are named here because LinkML's Pydantic generator ignores extra_slots, so without them the Pydantic model refuses every SSVC decision."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "slots": [
        "nvdSsvcOption__exploitation",
        "nvdSsvcOption__automatable",
        "nvdSsvcOption__technicalImpact"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "exploitation",
          "description": "How far the vulnerability is known to be exploited, such as none, poc or active.",
          "any_of": [
            {
              "range": "string",
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            },
            {
              "range": "string",
              "multivalued": true,
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "automatable",
          "description": "Whether an attacker could automate the attack, as yes or no.",
          "notes": [
            "CVSS 4.0's Automatable differs from this key only by case, so the two share one page of the generated docs on a case-insensitive filesystem. Both are real keys, so neither is renamed, and tests/test_schema_rules.py pins this as the one such pair."
          ],
          "any_of": [
            {
              "range": "string",
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            },
            {
              "range": "string",
              "multivalued": true,
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "technicalImpact",
          "description": "How much control an attacker would gain, as partial or total.",
          "any_of": [
            {
              "range": "string",
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            },
            {
              "range": "string",
              "multivalued": true,
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcOption",
      "extra_slots": {
        "range_expression": {
          "any_of": [
            {
              "range": "string",
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            },
            {
              "range": "string",
              "multivalued": true,
              "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
            }
          ],
          "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
        },
        "@type": "ExtraSlotsExpression"
      },
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdSsvcDecisionTree",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdSsvcDecisionTree",
      "description": "A whole SSVC decision tree, in the form of the schema NVD's file names.",
      "comments": [
        "NVD's file refers to a schema at democert.org for this object, and this project does not render that schema. No record of the modified feed of 2026-11-03 holds a decision tree, and tests/test_upstream.py lists the departure."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "linkml:Any"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Any",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdAffected",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffected",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "cve_api_json_2.0.schema#/definitions/affected",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The products that one source says the vulnerability affects.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "aliases": [
        "affected"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "NvdAffected_source",
        "nvdAffected__affectedData"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "affectedData",
          "description": "The products.",
          "range": "NvdAffectedProduct",
          "required": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "inlined_as_list": true,
          "minimum_cardinality": 1,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffected",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdAffectedProduct",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffectedProduct",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "cve_affected_1.0.json#",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "A product and which of its versions have the vulnerability.",
      "notes": [
        "NVD's file has the same keys as the CVE Record Format's product. It drops the two rules that the CVE format states, that a product names a vendor and product or a collection and package, and that it has versions or a default status, so this class does not state them. The default status keeps NVD's own enum beside it, so nvd_cve needs no second copy of the CVE module."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "close_mappings": [
        "cve:CveProduct"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "defaultStatus",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__vendor",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__product",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__collectionURL",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__packageName",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__cpes",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__modules",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__programFiles",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__programRoutines",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__platforms",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__repo",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__versions",
        "nvdAffectedProduct__packageURL"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "vendor",
          "description": "Who makes or maintains the product.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:vendor"
          ],
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,512}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "product",
          "description": "The product's name.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:product"
          ],
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,2048}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "collectionURL",
          "description": "The address of the package collection that holds the product.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:collectionURL"
          ],
          "range": "uri",
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,2048}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "packageName",
          "description": "The package's name within that collection.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:packageName"
          ],
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,2048}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "cpes",
          "description": "The product's CPE names, in the 2.2 or the 2.3 form.",
          "comments": [
            "NVD's own pattern, with its quotes written as \\x22 and \\x27, which mean the same. The Python generators cut a raw string at a quote."
          ],
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:cpes"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "pattern": "([c][pP][eE]:/[AHOaho]?(:[A-Za-z0-9._\\-~%]*){0,6})|(cpe:2\\.3:[aho*\\-](:(((\\?*|\\*?)([a-zA-Z0-9\\-._]|(\\\\[\\\\*?!\\x22#$%&\\x27()+,/:;<=>@\\[\\]\\^`{|}~]))+(\\?*|\\*?))|[*\\-])){5}(:(([a-zA-Z]{2,3}(-([a-zA-Z]{2}|[0-9]{3}))?)|[*\\-]))(:(((\\?*|\\*?)([a-zA-Z0-9\\-._]|(\\\\[\\\\*?!\\x22#$%&\\x27()+,/:;<=>@\\[\\]\\^`{|}~]))+(\\?*|\\*?))|[*\\-])){4})",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "modules",
          "description": "The affected parts of the product.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:modules"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,4096}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "programFiles",
          "description": "The affected source code files.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:programFiles"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,1024}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "programRoutines",
          "description": "The affected source code routines.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:programRoutines"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "range": "NvdProgramRoutine",
          "multivalued": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "inlined_as_list": true,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "platforms",
          "description": "The platforms the vulnerability is limited to.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:platforms"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "multivalued": true,
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{0,1024}$",
          "minimum_cardinality": 1,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "repo",
          "description": "The address of the product's source code repository.",
          "comments": [
            "NVD's file says format uri. Some records write an address that RFC 3986 refuses, such as git://git@gitlab.com:gitlab-org/gitlab.git, so this is a string and tests/test_upstream.py lists the departure."
          ],
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:repo"
          ],
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,2048}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "versions",
          "description": "The versions or ranges of versions whose status is known.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:versions"
          ],
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "range": "NvdAffectedVersion",
          "multivalued": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "inlined_as_list": true,
          "minimum_cardinality": 1,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "packageURL",
          "description": "The product's Package URL, with no version in it.",
          "close_mappings": [
            "cve:packageURL"
          ],
          "range": "uri",
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,2048}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffectedProduct",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdProgramRoutine",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdProgramRoutine",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "cve_affected_1.0.json#/properties/programRoutines/items",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "One affected source code routine.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "close_mappings": [
        "cve:CveProgramRoutine"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdProgramRoutine",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NvdAffectedVersion",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffectedVersion",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "upstream_definition",
          "value": "cve_affected_1.0.json#/properties/versions/items",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The status of one version of a product, or of a range of its versions.",
      "notes": [
        "These four rules state the oneOf of NVD's file, which has four branches: a version and a status alone, those with a numbering scheme, and those with a scheme and one of the two limits."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve",
      "close_mappings": [
        "cve:CveProductVersion"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "NvdAffectedVersion_version",
        "NvdAffectedVersion_status",
        "nvdAffectedVersion__versionType",
        "nvdAffectedVersion__lessThan",
        "nvdAffectedVersion__lessThanOrEqual",
        "nvdAffectedVersion__changes"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "versionType",
          "description": "The numbering scheme that orders the versions, such as semver or git.",
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,128}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "lessThan",
          "description": "The first version after the range.",
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,1024}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "lessThanOrEqual",
          "description": "The last version in the range.",
          "pattern": "^[\\s\\S]{1,1024}$",
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        },
        {
          "name": "changes",
          "description": "Where the status changes within the range.",
          "list_elements_unique": true,
          "range": "NvdVersionChange",
          "multivalued": true,
          "inlined": true,
          "inlined_as_list": true,
          "minimum_cardinality": 1,
          "@type": "SlotDefinition"
        }
      ],
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffectedVersion",
      "rules": [
        {
          "preconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "lessThan",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "postconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "versionType",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "description": "A range with a less-than limit names the numbering scheme.",
          "@type": "ClassRule"
        },
        {
          "preconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "lessThanOrEqual",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "postconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "versionType",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "description": "A range with a less-than-or-equal limit names the numbering scheme.",
          "@type": "ClassRule"
        },
        {
          "preconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "lessThan",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "postconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "lessThanOrEqual",
                "value_presence": "ABSENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "description": "A range has one upper limit, not two.",
          "@type": "ClassRule"
        },
        {
          "preconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "changes",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              },
              {
                "name": "lessThan",
                "value_presence": "ABSENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "postconditions": {
            "slot_conditions": [
              {
                "name": "lessThanOrEqual",
                "value_presence": "PRESENT",
                "@type": "SlotDefinition"
              }
            ],
            "@type": "AnonymousClassExpression"
          },
          "description": "Status changes belong to a range, so they need an upper limit.",
          "@type": "ClassRule"
        }
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
